agent: Let a key waiting on its PIN hold up nothing else

The agent held its one lock for the whole of a signature, and
go-tpm-keyfiles holds another, shared by every signature, while it asks
for the PIN. So a PIN prompt nobody answered held up every request to the
agent, for every key: one program using a key whose PIN wasn't typed this
session froze every SSH login and signed commit until someone came to the
screen, 21 minutes one night.

Ask for the PIN, and the confirmation, before taking either lock, and hand
the signer what came back. The agent's lock is held only to find the key.

Stop an askpass nobody answers after a minute, with a TERM it can take
its prompt down on, and count it as unanswered. Ask for one key's PIN or
confirmation one prompt at a time, and refuse a key whose prompt, either
kind, went unanswered for ten minutes without another, saying which key
and until when, so a program trying it all night puts up one prompt
rather than one a minute. The journal names the key each prompt is for,
and for a confirmation the process asking.

